Variable x:𝖤𝗅𝖾𝗆𝖾𝗇𝗍

Theorem (UnionOfEmptyCollectionsIsEmpty)
  ∅ ∪ ∅ = ∅
  Proof
    (x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∪ ∅) 𝗂𝖿𝖿 (x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∨ x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅) by UnionOfCollections
    ¬(x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅) by EmptyCollections
    ¬(x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∨ x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅) by NegatedDikjunctionIdempotence
    ¬(x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∪ ∅) 𝗂𝖿𝖿 ¬(x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∨ x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅) by BiconditionalContraposition
    ¬(x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∪ ∅) by BiconditionalImplicationRightElimination
    (x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∪ ∅) 𝗂𝖿𝖿 (x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅) by EquivalenceOfFalsities
    (∅ ∪ ∅ = ∅) 𝗂𝖿𝖿 (x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∪ ∅ 𝗂𝖿𝖿 x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅) by Extensionality
  Therefore
    ∅ ∪ ∅ = ∅ by BiconditionalImplicationRightElimination

Theorem (IntersectionOfEmptyCollectionsIsEmpty)
  ∅ ∩ ∅ = ∅
  Proof
    (x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∩ ∅) 𝗂𝖿𝖿 (x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∧ x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅) by IntersectionOfCollections
    ¬(x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅) by EmptyCollections
    ¬(x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∧ x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅) by NegatedConjunctionIdempotence
    ¬(x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∩ ∅) 𝗂𝖿𝖿 ¬(x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∧ x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅) by BiconditionalContraposition
    ¬(x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∩ ∅) by BiconditionalImplicationRightElimination
    (x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∩ ∅) 𝗂𝖿𝖿 (x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅) by EquivalenceOfFalsities
    (∅ ∩ ∅ = ∅) 𝗂𝖿𝖿 (x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅ ∩ ∅ 𝗂𝖿𝖿 x is an 𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘰𝘧 ∅) by Extensionality
  Therefore
    ∅ ∩ ∅ = ∅ by BiconditionalImplicationRightElimination
